From 6c0c9da8ef0870bfb9ecce4f629db1a763f0c481 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hung Fan Lin <leolin84200704@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 11:25:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [VP-17868] Say which consult already used the accession
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"The Accession ID selected has been used." does not say when it was used,
so a provider whose accession is held by a consult that already happened
(the normal case — a claim is only released on cancel / delete /
accession swap, never when the consult takes place) goes looking through
their upcoming consults, finds nothing, and files a ticket.

Show the consult date when transv2 discloses it, fall back to wording
that says past consults count too, and point at Support, which is where
the unlock actually lives: resetEventAccession is exposed to admin /
clinicadmin / clinical team, and its only UI is the internal wellness
portal — nothing in this portal can release a claim.

The alert also loses its hard 42px height: the longer copy wraps to two
or three lines and a fixed box clipped it.

supportEmail is interpolated instead of baked into the message because
vue-i18n reads "@" in a message body as linked-message syntax.
